OL,3,GNEWSASurvivor, 102, recalls tragedy
OL,4,Athat killed 464 men
OL,5,
OL,6,FA 102-year-old survivor of the sinking
OL,7,Fof a ship in World War Two has
OL,8,Fdescribed spending more than four hours
OL,9,Fin oil-covered water as he waited to be
OL,10,Frescued.
OL,12,FRoyal Navy cruiser HMS Charybdis was
OL,13,Ftorpedoed off Guernsey by German
OL,14,FE-boats on 23 October 1943.
OL,16,FJohn Eskdale, from Lydney in
OL,17,FGloucestershire, was 19 and serving as
OL,18,Fa Royal Marine when the ship sank, with
OL,19,F464 members of the crew losing their
OL,20,Flives and 107 being rescued.
